# Server Environments

Software is usually deployed in different environments before reaching users.

## 1. Development Server

Used by developers.

Purpose:

- Write code
- Test new features
- Fix bugs

---

## 2. QA (Quality Assurance) Server

Used by testers.

Purpose:

- Execute test cases
- Verify functionality
- Report bugs

---

## 3. Production Server

Used by end users.

Purpose:

- Live application
- Accessible to customers

---

# Role of Testers

Testers are responsible for ensuring software quality.

Responsibilities:

- Prepare test cases
- Execute testing
- Report defects
- Verify bug fixes
- Approve software for deployment

---

# HR Team Responsibilities

Human Resources (HR) manages employee-related activities.

Responsibilities:

- Recruitment
- Interviews
- Salary discussions
- Employee onboarding
- Company policies
- Performance management

---

# IT Team Responsibilities

The IT team manages the organization's technical infrastructure.

Responsibilities:

- Database management
- Server management
- Network support
- User access management
- Internal system maintenance

---

# Product Manager

The Product Manager focuses on **what should be built**.

Responsibilities:

- Define product vision
- Create product roadmap
- Gather customer requirements
- Prioritize features
- Work closely with stakeholders

---

# Project Manager

The Project Manager focuses on **how and when the project will be delivered**.

Responsibilities:

- Project planning
- Timeline management
- Resource allocation
- Team coordination
- Risk management
- Ensure timely delivery

